course: dictionary
lesson: 6724
title: Often and how often
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Often means many times. If you often play outside, you play outside a lot. The words around it give clues: «I often walk to school» tells you it happens on most days, not just once.
explain: «How often» is a question about how many times something happens in a time, like each day or each week. «Every 15 minutes» is an answer to «How often does the bus come?»
explain: Often has forms you can use. More often and most often compare how many times something happens. «Older children in big families often help a lot, but they still need sleep» means helping happens many times, not every time.
fact: Often means many times.
fact: «How often» asks how many times something happens in a time, like each day or each week.
fact: Often has forms: more often, most often, and the older form oftener.
fact: «Every so often» means now and then, from time to time.
fact: «Older children in big families often help a lot, but they still need breakfast, sleep and time for themselves.»
exercise: «I often walk to school.» What does often mean here? | *Many times | Once only | Very slowly | Never
exercise: Ella asks, «How often does the bus come?» Which answer fits? | Because it is raining | Yesterday at lunch | *Every 15 minutes | It is big and red
exercise: Find and copy the word in «Albino animals often see poorly» that means many times. | *often | animals | poorly | albino
test: Lily visits the library ___ than Sam, so she knows more books. Which word fits the gap? | every so often | how often | most often | *more often
test: Which question asks how many times something happens each week? | Who swims with you? | *How often do you swim? | Is swimming fun? | Where do you swim?
exam: Mia says, «I often read before bed.» What does often tell us? | *Something happens many times | Something happens once only | Something never happens | Something is very loud
